spec:
  grid: 11-12 rows x 11-12 cols, single bg color filling most cells
  colors: 3 distinct -- bg (dominant), wall, marker (all different)
  marker:
    count: exactly 1 pixel
    position: inside the wall band, on an empty or wall row; col strictly between wall boundaries on rows that have both sides
  wall:
    pixel_count: 8-14
    rows: 4-6 rows carry wall pixels; they span a contiguous band of 5-7 rows with 1-2 empty interior rows
    per_row: 1-4 wall pixels per wall row; each side (left/right of marker col) forms a contiguous horizontal block of 1-2 pixels
    shape: passage narrows at band endpoints and widens toward the center (lens/funnel); left boundary decreases then increases, right boundary increases then decreases; same-side wall pixels on adjacent wall rows must 8-connect (column step <= 1)
    openings: exactly the intended top/bottom/left/right gaps may separate wall arcs; wall pixels form exactly four 8-connected components and no extra breaks inside adjacent same-side wall rows
    one_sided: some wall rows may have wall only on one side of marker col (passage extends to grid edge) [observed]
    vertical_symmetry: wall pattern is vertically symmetric around band center [observed, not always exact]
  band_padding:
    rows_above_top_wall: 2 [observed]
    rows_below_bot_wall: 3-4
  output_same_size: true
  transform: |
    On each wall row, fill bg pixels between nearest left wall (exclusive) and nearest right wall (exclusive) with marker color; one-sided rows fill to grid edge.
    Empty rows inside band get full-width fill.
    Rows outside band reuse the nearest endpoint wall-row interval.
    Wall pixels and original marker pixel are preserved.

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (constraints are easy to satisfy forward)
  steps:
    - Pick grid size 11-12 x 11-12, choose 3 distinct colors for bg/wall/marker
    - Choose marker column (3-8, leaving room for walls on both sides)
